                <pb facs="1115" n="979" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg979"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No.
                    226.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Messrs. Hillion, de Sesmaisons, and Zohrabto the
                        Revolutionary Committee at Cape Haytien.</hi></head>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#italic">To the Gentlemen Members of the
                        Committee of Cape Hayti:</hi></p>
                <p>The undersigned, Monseignor Hillion, Archbishop of Port au Prince; Messrs the
                    Comte de Sesmaisons, minister plenipotentiary of France in Hayti; Zohrab,
                    consul-general of England for Hayti and San Domingo, have the honor te inform
                    you that, for the purpose of reconciliation outside of all political party, and
                    as sincere friends of the country, they have come to the Cape to propose to you
                    the most proper means to avoid effusion of blood.</p>
                <p>Mr. Margron, charged with the portfolio of exterior relations, accompanies them
                    provided with full powers.</p>
                <p>The undersigned, in order to assure the calm and the security of deliberations,
                    invite you to have no objections to come on board the French cruiser <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bisson</hi>, neutral ground, according to international
                    laws.</p>
                <p>They would be happy to receive a prompt answer, considering the necessity for the
                    ship to leave the Cape without delay.</p>
                <closer><dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Harbor of Cape Hayti</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-11-21"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 21,
                        1888</date>.</dateline></closer>
            </div>
